WEBVTT

00:24.448 --> 00:27.993
That's it. I'm gonna become a musician.

00:30.412 --> 00:32.122
What kind of nonsense is that?

00:42.549 --> 00:44.760
Get a clue. You're in fourth grade now.

00:44.843 --> 00:46.762
Nah, I'm gonna be a musician for real.

00:46.845 --> 00:51.183
I'll work part-time, buy a guitar,
and make 100 songs before high school!

00:51.266 --> 00:53.769
You sound like a fool.
That was a vintage guitar.

00:53.852 --> 00:56.146
Do you have any idea how much those cost?

00:59.524 --> 01:00.984
Superstar, coming through!

01:01.068 --> 01:02.778
Toshiro Kamiya on vocals,

01:02.861 --> 01:04.905
and Yomiko Horai on bass!

01:06.031 --> 01:07.199
Forget it.

01:12.287 --> 01:13.622
I'm not doing it.

01:23.048 --> 01:27.094
I'm hungry. I wonder what Mom's
gonna make for dinner.

01:30.055 --> 01:31.598
What's wrong, Yomiko?

01:36.394 --> 01:38.355
I'm transferring to another school.

01:38.438 --> 01:40.357
Yomiko?

01:40.440 --> 01:43.693
<i>It's been 100 years</i>
<i>since thick clouds blocked out the sun.</i>

01:44.528 --> 01:47.489
<i>This endless winter night</i>
<i>killed off almost every plant.</i>

01:47.572 --> 01:51.535
<i>To survive in a world like this,</i>
<i>humans developed a certain technology.</i>

01:52.118 --> 01:53.453
<i>Transfloration.</i>

01:53.537 --> 01:56.289
<i>Near-death human bodies</i>
<i>are implanted with a seed.</i>

01:56.373 --> 01:59.292
<i>Then, a plant sprouts</i>
<i>by feeding off the host's soul.</i>

01:59.376 --> 02:02.045
<i>About two years</i>
<i>after the Transfloration Procedure,</i>

02:02.129 --> 02:06.925
<i>the humans become "Spiriflora"</i>
<i>living as trees, houseplants, or flowers.</i>

02:07.008 --> 02:11.638
<i>Even under minimal lighting, they produce</i>
<i>ample oxygen to keep everyone alive.</i>

02:12.764 --> 02:15.308
- Yomiko, got enough forceps?
- Yeah, I'm good.

02:16.101 --> 02:18.228
Okay, done. Just stitch that up.

02:22.691 --> 02:24.734
Feels like murder, doesn't it?

02:24.818 --> 02:27.279
What? If anything,
we're prolonging his life.

02:27.362 --> 02:30.448
He was at death's door.
As a human, he only had a month left.

02:30.532 --> 02:33.160
Can living as a plant
even be considered "living"?

02:33.243 --> 02:34.995
I couldn't care less.

02:35.078 --> 02:37.873
Patients undergo the procedure
at their own discretion.

02:37.956 --> 02:43.628
The ten million-yen transfloration subsidy
makes their final two years comfortable.

03:04.774 --> 03:07.485
I know. I know everything.

03:07.569 --> 03:10.864
I'm the only one.
Yes, I'm the only one who knows.

03:10.947 --> 03:15.035
I won't lose to them.
I swear I won't lose, I swear…

03:15.118 --> 03:16.536
<i>Yesterday was the last dose…</i>

03:16.620 --> 03:17.787
I swear… I swear…

03:17.871 --> 03:19.831
<i>Gotta get some more.</i>

03:29.591 --> 03:33.887
<i>I work 14-hour shifts at the factory</i>
<i>for a monthly salary of 90,000 yen.</i>

03:33.970 --> 03:36.806
<i>I pay 30,000 for rent</i>
<i>and 5,000 for utilities.</i>

03:36.890 --> 03:40.101
<i>Then, 15,000 in taxes</i>
<i>and 20,000 for my mom's medication.</i>

03:40.185 --> 03:42.145
<i>Less than 20,000 yen left over.</i>

03:42.229 --> 03:45.357
<i>My multiple welfare applications</i>
<i>have all been rejected.</i>

03:47.484 --> 03:49.778
<i>Patrolling already? No freaking way.</i>

03:57.619 --> 04:01.331
<i>Crap, crap, crap.</i>
<i>I've made no progress. Gotta hurry.</i>

04:04.876 --> 04:08.380
<i>I scrimp on food expenses</i>
<i>to save 1,000 yen each month.</i>

04:08.463 --> 04:10.340
<i>Money for my job hunt.</i>

04:10.423 --> 04:14.094
<i>For a new job, I need education.</i>
<i>For education, I gotta pay tuition.</i>

04:14.928 --> 04:18.556
<i>I can't stay here.</i>
<i>If I don't find a new job, I'm gonna die.</i>

04:20.058 --> 04:24.187
<i>After three years working here,</i>
<i>I've saved 20,000 yen.</i>

04:25.981 --> 04:27.190
Ouch!

04:38.410 --> 04:40.912
You're not getting paid today.

05:01.349 --> 05:03.560
Abolish the transfloration policy!

05:03.643 --> 05:07.522
Abolish transfloration!
Abolish transfloration!

05:09.607 --> 05:12.277
Abolish transfloration!

05:13.570 --> 05:14.404
MENTAL HEALTH CLINIC

05:14.487 --> 05:15.989
Please, I beg of you.

05:16.072 --> 05:19.242
Without her drugs, she goes berserk.
I swear I'll pay you.

05:19.326 --> 05:22.954
When she flips, there's no stopping her.
I'm begging you.

05:24.581 --> 05:28.126
You said that last week, too.

05:29.002 --> 05:30.545
Get out.

05:53.651 --> 05:56.321
<i>The tuition money I was hiding…</i>

05:56.404 --> 05:58.865
You lied… You liar…

05:58.948 --> 06:01.701
You lied to me. You had money all along.

06:01.785 --> 06:03.953
Mom, don't get the wrong idea!

06:04.037 --> 06:05.371
You're full of crap!

06:05.455 --> 06:08.041
Everyone's out to get me.
But I won't lose… I…

06:08.124 --> 06:11.169
I was gonna use that money
to pay for high school, and…

06:11.252 --> 06:13.171
No excuses!

06:48.289 --> 06:51.960
<i>Why? What did I do to deserve this?</i>

06:53.211 --> 06:55.547
<i>Why am I the only one</i>
<i>suffering all the time?</i>

06:57.048 --> 06:59.008
<i>What am I supposed to do?</i>

07:22.532 --> 07:24.993
So many protests lately, huh?

07:25.076 --> 07:29.247
If you ask me, they should
protest working conditions instead.

07:29.330 --> 07:31.833
So that detectives like me
can get paid overtime…

07:33.918 --> 07:35.336
It's a parent and child.

07:35.420 --> 07:37.380
Any traces of the murderer?

07:37.464 --> 07:39.382
Nothing at all.

07:39.466 --> 07:41.634
It's bizarre, honestly.

07:43.470 --> 07:47.223
<i>I was asked to help with a case</i>
<i>supposedly linked to transfloration.</i>

07:47.307 --> 07:50.727
<i>The others turned me down,</i>
<i>but success requires arduous--</i>

07:50.810 --> 07:53.104
I'll do it. As long as I get paid.

07:54.105 --> 07:55.773
<i>- Thanks…</i>
- Okay, bye now.

07:55.857 --> 07:58.443
I'm being called to the transfloration
reception desk.

08:03.490 --> 08:06.826
Getting ten million yen
without having to work must be nice…

08:11.539 --> 08:14.000
Let's wrap this up
and find something good to eat!

08:17.754 --> 08:19.047
Hello.

08:19.964 --> 08:20.924
It's cold in here…

08:31.559 --> 08:33.728
Wait, are you…

08:49.994 --> 08:51.079
TRANSFLORATION REGISTRATION

08:51.162 --> 08:52.413
How long has it been?

08:55.250 --> 08:57.752
About 15 years, I guess…

08:58.419 --> 09:00.838
That's because you never had a phone.

09:02.131 --> 09:03.675
Are you really dying?

09:04.259 --> 09:06.844
Gotta be dying
to qualify for transfloration, right?

09:08.137 --> 09:09.931
There's my doctor's note.

09:11.057 --> 09:12.976
SMALL BOWEL CANCER, STAGE IV

09:14.477 --> 09:18.565
Hurry up and plant a seed in me
so I can become a pretty flower.

09:20.400 --> 09:24.195
First, we'll do a basic examination
to verify your medical certificate.

09:37.667 --> 09:39.460
Did someone attack you?

09:40.795 --> 09:43.506
These streets are getting rough, huh?

09:43.590 --> 09:45.258
But I guess that's nothing new.

09:45.341 --> 09:46.676
I'm fine.

09:53.975 --> 09:56.394
SAVE THE WORLD WITH TRANSFLORATION!

10:08.281 --> 10:11.701
Toshiro, Yomiko, who did this to you?

10:11.784 --> 10:13.745
I'm gonna kill that old man.

10:15.163 --> 10:18.750
Why are the adults in this world
so angry all the time?

10:18.833 --> 10:20.001
I'm tired of it…

10:21.169 --> 10:23.546
Those clouds
cast darkness over our hearts.

10:23.630 --> 10:27.300
By rejecting everyone else,
we narrow our own perspective.

10:28.176 --> 10:31.929
This might be hard to comprehend,
but you must avoid the same fate

10:32.013 --> 10:35.933
by making sure your heart stays content.

10:36.017 --> 10:37.560
I don't understand.

10:37.644 --> 10:38.978
I'll kill that old geezer!

10:53.159 --> 10:55.912
Why'd you lie about having cancer?!

10:55.995 --> 10:58.247
Because you don't take suicidal patients.

10:58.331 --> 11:02.627
Your blood contained over 150 types
of chemical substances and bacteria!

11:02.710 --> 11:05.588
You drank industrial wastewater
to get your hands on that subsidy?

11:05.672 --> 11:07.131
Go to the hospital right now.

11:07.215 --> 11:10.009
Getting dialysis
to clean your organs might save you!

11:12.220 --> 11:13.346
Come on!

11:13.429 --> 11:17.058
Can't afford that.
I'm not a government worker like you.

11:17.141 --> 11:20.228
What's the problem?
There must be tons of people like me.

11:20.311 --> 11:21.938
Just gimme a stamp of approval.

11:22.021 --> 11:25.817
I gotta pay for that doctor's note later.
I can't even afford to eat today.

11:25.900 --> 11:27.443
If you die, that won't matter!

11:27.527 --> 11:30.113
It's transfloration.
I ain't gonna die yet.

11:30.196 --> 11:32.407
I'm tired of worrying about money.

11:32.490 --> 11:34.409
Is that what you want?!

11:34.492 --> 11:36.536
You'll just be fertilizer
for the plants to grow!

11:36.619 --> 11:39.163
Paralyzed with their minds fully intact!

11:39.247 --> 11:41.916
They mumble words,
but it's all just gibberish.

11:41.999 --> 11:45.169
For all we know,
they might be suffering for all eternity!

11:45.253 --> 11:48.589
I'll spend that ten million
to make my heart content!

11:52.468 --> 11:54.345
What kind of nonsense is that?

11:55.221 --> 11:58.224
There's nothing fun about being alive.

12:08.526 --> 12:09.527
Please.

12:30.047 --> 12:34.760
Hey, did we end up letting Toshiro Kamiya
undergo transfloration the other day?

12:34.844 --> 12:35.970
Kamiya?

12:37.680 --> 12:41.517
Oh, it looks like
his procedure concluded five days ago.

12:41.601 --> 12:42.894
I see.

12:55.281 --> 12:56.282
Rain…

12:58.659 --> 13:02.079
Yeah, well, it's been a while,
so I wanted to check in.

13:02.163 --> 13:04.707
Let's get some food sometime. Seeya.

13:18.471 --> 13:19.805
Huh? Yomiko?

13:21.891 --> 13:23.976
What happened?

13:24.977 --> 13:27.730
All the money got stolen…

14:41.387 --> 14:42.388
Yum…

14:43.097 --> 14:45.766
Can't remember the last time I had meat…

14:47.393 --> 14:48.561
How much is this?

14:48.644 --> 14:50.897
It's on me. Don't worry about it.

14:52.899 --> 14:55.192
This makes my heart content.

15:00.615 --> 15:03.576
Rich government workers
live in a different world, huh?

15:08.080 --> 15:11.208
By the way, is my blood gonna be okay?

15:11.292 --> 15:14.921
Yeah, I think the seed
washed out that industrial wastewater.

15:15.671 --> 15:18.257
Seeds work really well
to repair their hosts.

15:18.341 --> 15:21.385
Want a checkup
at Transflora Medical tomorrow?

15:21.469 --> 15:23.262
We can eat out again afterward.

15:23.346 --> 15:25.598
You don't gotta feel bad for me.

15:25.681 --> 15:27.516
That's not why I offered…

15:28.142 --> 15:29.560
The guys behind you said so.

15:30.478 --> 15:34.148
They sensed feelings of
self-blame and regret coming from you.

15:37.109 --> 15:40.529
You understand what Spiriflora are saying?

15:41.948 --> 15:44.408
It's a side effect
of transfloration, isn't it?

15:44.492 --> 15:46.786
No, I've never heard of that.

15:47.662 --> 15:48.829
How do you…

15:48.913 --> 15:52.750
Now they're saying…
you're hopeful about something.

15:52.833 --> 15:54.377
Toshiro.

15:54.460 --> 15:56.796
Let's go to Transflora Medical. Now.

16:29.203 --> 16:30.329
What, no checkup?

16:32.373 --> 16:33.958
Hello, there.

16:34.834 --> 16:37.086
I'm Jin Hiragishi of the Unsection.

16:38.838 --> 16:40.631
Unsection?

16:40.715 --> 16:44.552
An unaffiliated section
covering anything transfloration-related.

16:44.635 --> 16:45.970
He's a big shot there.

16:46.637 --> 16:48.305
I'm Toshiro Kamiya.

16:48.389 --> 16:50.975
So, you can hear the Spiriflora?

16:51.058 --> 16:52.518
You told him?

16:52.601 --> 16:56.188
When a Spiriflor is nearby,
he can hear the human inside them.

16:56.272 --> 16:58.399
He's invaluable to our organization.

16:58.482 --> 17:00.484
And potentially useful for "that" case.

17:02.403 --> 17:04.030
What's this all about?

17:04.113 --> 17:07.366
We're talking about
hiring you as a temporary worker.

17:08.701 --> 17:12.371
It's two years of stable pay
working here while you're still human.

17:12.455 --> 17:14.373
Not a bad deal, right?

17:14.457 --> 17:17.793
Yeah, at this point,
I'll do anything for money.

17:17.877 --> 17:19.920
I haven't agreed to this yet.

17:20.004 --> 17:22.548
You can't expect me
to hire you right off the bat.

17:22.631 --> 17:23.924
Is your ability legit?

17:24.008 --> 17:28.512
Yeah, pretty much. But I can't hear words.
It's like… vibes they pick up from us.

17:28.596 --> 17:32.808
Do Spiriflora even have a personality?
What do they say when nobody's around?

17:32.892 --> 17:34.894
They all say different stuff.

17:35.770 --> 17:38.731
Some just yell randomly,
some are thirsty, and so on.

17:38.814 --> 17:42.943
But I can't hear anything from Spiriflora
who transitioned too long ago.

17:45.362 --> 17:47.531
What do they sense from me right now?

17:48.908 --> 17:53.370
Bewilderment, expectation…
and resignation.

17:54.163 --> 17:54.997
Also…

17:55.956 --> 17:57.249
self-admonition.

17:59.668 --> 18:00.669
Come with me.

18:04.256 --> 18:05.132
Where to?

18:05.216 --> 18:07.635
Do a Spiriflor's words
translate automatically in your head?

18:09.011 --> 18:10.596
No, it doesn't work like that.

18:10.679 --> 18:14.183
It's more like an impulsive thing
that they express through sounds.

18:16.811 --> 18:19.063
What's our associate here saying?

18:19.146 --> 18:21.732
Yelling about something, right?

18:21.816 --> 18:23.609
It's not like I can decipher every…

18:29.698 --> 18:31.408
Sorry. I don't know.

18:31.492 --> 18:34.703
It should be saying something.
If you can hear it, I'll hire you.

18:35.454 --> 18:37.164
Don't make something up.

18:37.248 --> 18:41.669
I don't need an ability like yours
to know whether someone's lying.

18:45.756 --> 18:47.675
<i>What if I can't hear it?</i>

18:47.758 --> 18:49.426
<i>What if he doesn't hire me?</i>

18:49.510 --> 18:52.346
<i>How am I gonna survive</i>
<i>another day in that house?</i>

19:19.415 --> 19:20.791
<i>I got no choice but to listen!</i>

19:22.877 --> 19:24.211
<i>Listen.</i>

19:27.006 --> 19:28.215
<i>Listen.</i>

19:29.049 --> 19:30.467
<i>Listen harder.</i>

19:33.554 --> 19:34.847
<i>Concentrate.</i>

20:02.208 --> 20:05.753
<i>Head… for…</i>

20:05.836 --> 20:07.755
"Head for…"

20:08.756 --> 20:10.132
<i>Antarctica…</i>

20:11.091 --> 20:12.384
"Antarctica…"

20:18.724 --> 20:20.809
You need a place to sleep, huh?

20:22.770 --> 20:25.814
- Come here at the same time tomorrow.
- What?

20:26.523 --> 20:28.275
Oh, okay, thank you.

20:47.294 --> 20:49.755
What happened? Tissues, tissues!

20:49.838 --> 20:52.800
My head's cracking…
What was that feeling just now?

20:52.883 --> 20:54.218
I'll never do that again!

20:55.844 --> 21:00.641
Including that unpaid amount from before,
your total comes to 35,000 yen.

21:08.691 --> 21:10.776
ORAL MEDICATION
KAORI KAMIYA

21:10.859 --> 21:13.279
I'm sorry for all the trouble.

21:14.571 --> 21:17.533
As long as you pay up,
I have no complaints.

21:39.263 --> 21:40.931
Are you okay with this?

21:41.015 --> 21:43.976
- What?
- Spending your money on that.

21:46.770 --> 21:49.815
Are you leaving now
to give your mom those drugs?

21:54.194 --> 21:55.821
So, how much am I getting paid?

21:56.989 --> 21:58.240
As a Special Temporary Worker,

21:58.324 --> 22:01.035
you get a base salary of 150,000 yen
plus commission.

22:01.118 --> 22:02.745
That's double my old salary.

22:04.913 --> 22:06.749
I can eat out every day now.

22:07.833 --> 22:11.128
I really wanted to try
one of those "kebab" things.

22:12.796 --> 22:14.006
Toshiro…

22:14.590 --> 22:15.716
And…

22:17.092 --> 22:18.302
And…

22:19.887 --> 22:21.096
Oh, no!

23:04.848 --> 23:05.766
Let's go.

23:12.147 --> 23:13.232
Thanks.

24:37.941 --> 24:42.946
Subtitle translation by: Logan Lampkins
